# Header: replaces patch 0012's time window, which skipped a host event
# for any name this guest had changed within two seconds and so could
# hide a Mac-side edit that followed the guest's own. An event is now
# skipped only when it provably reports the guest's own change: a removed
# name that is already negative here, or a name whose inode this guest
# changed and whose LOOKUP returns the same node with the cached size,
# mtime and ctime. Any other same-node event refreshes the attributes from
# that reply and is raised in place, keeping the dentry. A new kind, s
# (rescan), reports that the host lost events: the connection epoch is
# bumped, and on virtiofs a stale-epoch dentry is revalidated with a
# LOOKUP rather than dropped, so mounts on unchanged directories stay
# attached; directories made here stop answering missing names without a
# request.
